entry.summary:
I like Tortoise ORM. Django-style models, async-first, clean. But I wanted more speed on read-heavy paths without reaching for SQLAlchemy, so I built yara-orm: a Tortoise-style async ORM where the model and query layer is Python, but the engine — connection pooling, parameter binding, and row decoding — is written in Rust (PyO3 over tokio-postgres and rusqlite). The API is exactly what you'd expect: from yara_orm import Model, YaraOrm, fields, in_transaction
class Author(Model): id = fields.IntField(pk=True) name = fields.CharField(max_length=100)
class Book(Model): id = fields.IntField(pk=True) title = fields.CharField(max_length=200) author = fields.ForeignKeyField("Author", related_name="books")
await YaraOrm.init("postgres://localhost/app") # or sqlite://./app.…
